1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,900
THE STUDENT OF PRAGUE made film history in 1913 as one of the first " artist films , "

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,900
for the premiere of which a score was composed .

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,900
The film was exported to many countries

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,800
and helped establish the worldwide reputation of German silent films .

5
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:18,800
Sadly , the film only survived in a re-edited version from 1926

6
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:22,600
and abridged English-language versions for foreign markets .

7
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:25,200
It wasn 't until 1987

8
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:29,100
that the first attempt at a reconstruction of the original version

9
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:33,000
was undertaken under the direction of Dr Wilfried Kugel .

10
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:39,000
This new digital reconstruction by the Filmmuseum München is based on the outline by Hanns Heinz Ewers ,

11
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:43,100
the original piano score by Josef Weiss and contemporary reviews .

12
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:47,200
The German intertitles have been re-set according to historical templates .

13
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:52,300
Judging from the duration listed by the censorship office in 1913 ( 1,548 metres , 85 minutes ) ,

14
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:56,400
the film is still missing roughly two minutes of footage .

15
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:01,500
The instances of missing pictures are replaced with short periods of black frames .

16
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:06,100
Musical prelude and interlude were already without pictures in the original .

17
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:38,000
The Student of Prague

18
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:42,300
A Romantic Drama in Four Acts by HANNS HEINZ EWERS .

19
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:46,500
Screenplay by the author .

20
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:50,800
- - Text translated and subtitles synced by darthfrede - -

21
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,800
CAST OF CHARACTERS :

22
00:01:53,900 --> 00:01:56,700
Balduin , a student

23
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:59,600
Scapinelli , an old adventurer

24
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:02,500
Lyduschka , a traveling girl

25
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:05,600
Countess Margit von Schwarzenberg

26
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:08,500
Count Schwarzenberg , her father

27
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:11,700
Baron Waldis-Schwarzenberg , her cousin and fiancé .

28
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:35,500
Author and leading actor in historical Prague , where the story will be played out .

29
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:20,700
ACT I.

30
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:09,600
" Long live Balduin ,

31
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:13,100
the best swordsman of Prague and its most audacious student ! "

32
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:16,900
" I 'm ruined !

33
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:21,000
If only I had a great fortune or a rich heiress . "

34
00:08:31,900 --> 00:08:37,700
Countess Margit and her fiancé set out on a par force hunt .

35
00:12:10,800 --> 00:12:13,500
" My dear cousin ,

36
00:12:13,700 --> 00:12:17,500
I will obey my father 's wishes , but I do not love you . "

37
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:37,800
The Countess slips her locket to Balduin .

38
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:29,100
Balduin 's student lodgings .

39
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:09,700
Balduin pays a visit to the Count .

40
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:10,800
I hereby certify that I was paid 100,000 guilder .

41
00:21:10,900 --> 00:21:14,700
In exchange , I give Mister Scapinelli

42
00:21:14,800 --> 00:21:18,600
the right to take from this room whatever pleases him .

43
00:21:18,700 --> 00:21:22,400
Prague , May 13 , 1820 .

44
00:22:37,800 --> 00:22:46,400
... the right to take from this room whatever pleases him .

45
00:22:46,500 --> 00:22:55,100
Prague , May 13 , 1820 . Balduin

46
00:25:00,800 --> 00:25:03,700
END OF ACT I.

47
00:25:04,200 --> 00:25:06,100
ACT II .

48
00:25:06,200 --> 00:25:12,500
Balduin is invited to a ball at the governor 's palace .

49
00:34:37,100 --> 00:34:39,100
" Who are you ? "

50
00:35:26,500 --> 00:35:29,900
I am no god nor a demon ,

51
00:35:30,000 --> 00:35:33,400
but the one who once scornfully called me by your name

52
00:35:33,500 --> 00:35:36,400
spoke the truth !

53
00:38:08,100 --> 00:38:12,500
The Countess in her drawing room .

54
00:38:43,300 --> 00:38:46,300
Countess , I beg you to keep your word !

55
00:38:46,400 --> 00:38:50,400
Eleven o 'clock tomorrow night , meet me at the Jewish Cemetery .

56
00:38:50,500 --> 00:38:54,500
It is the most secluded place in town and no one will see us there .

57
00:38:54,600 --> 00:38:56,600
Balduin

58
00:41:25,500 --> 00:41:28,800
END OF ACT II .

59
00:41:28,900 --> 00:42:24,000
Musical Interlude

60
00:42:24,500 --> 00:42:26,400
ACT III .

61
00:42:26,500 --> 00:42:30,400
Countess Margit leaves for the rendezvous .

62
00:52:47,500 --> 00:52:54,100
" With swords ? But Balduin is the best swordsman in Prague . "

63
00:54:46,800 --> 00:54:50,100
" Spare him !

64
00:54:50,200 --> 00:54:57,800
He is my sister 's only child , my daughter 's fiancé , my heir and the last to carry our name . "

65
00:55:51,600 --> 00:55:55,000
Balduin goes to the duel .

66
00:56:19,500 --> 00:56:24,500
The deed he would not commit , the other committed .

67
00:58:12,100 --> 00:58:15,100
END OF ACT III .

68
00:58:15,500 --> 00:58:17,500
ACT IV .

69
00:58:18,700 --> 00:58:26,000
Everywhere where I wanted to sleep , everywhere where I wanted to die ,

70
00:58:26,100 --> 00:58:33,400
everywhere where I waited another day , on my way I met a passer-by ,

71
00:58:33,500 --> 00:58:40,800
a pilgrim in everything black , resembling me like a brother !

72
00:58:40,900 --> 00:58:44,800
( Alfred de Musset )

73
00:58:45,700 --> 00:58:51,300
" Mister Balduin is no longer permitted to see the Count and the Lady . "

74
00:59:16,200 --> 00:59:21,400
Giving himself over to dance and play , Balduin seeks to forget his love .

75
01:02:36,100 --> 01:02:40,200
" Dare you also play against me ? "

76
01:03:46,800 --> 01:03:51,300
Balduin wants to see his beloved once more .

77
01:20:48,900 --> 01:20:53,600
I am no god nor a demon ,

78
01:20:53,700 --> 01:20:58,400
but the one who once scornfully called me by your name

79
01:20:58,500 --> 01:21:03,200
spoke the truth !

80
01:21:03,300 --> 01:21:08,000
Where you are , I too will always be ,

81
01:21:08,100 --> 01:21:12,800
and on your final hour , by the stone on your grave I will sit .

82
01:21:12,900 --> 01:21:15,500
( Alfred de Musset )

83
01:21:24,500 --> 01:21:52,500
Here lies Balduin

84
01:21:58,200 --> 01:22:01,500
The End .

